([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Molecular Weight Averages of Polymers]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A polymer sample consists of three monodisperse fractions:) Tj
T*
(Fraction 1: 100 molecules of molecular weight 10,000 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Fraction 2: 200 molecules of molecular weight 20,000 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Fraction 3: 100 molecules of molecular weight 50,000 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Calculate: \(1\) Number-Average Molecular Weight \(M_n\), \(2\) Weight-Average Molecular) Tj
T*
(Weight \(M_w\), \(3\) Polydispersity Index \(PDI\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Tabulate N_i and M_i:) Tj
T*
(Fraction 1: N1 = 100, M1 = 10,000 => N1*M1 = 1,000,000; N1*M1^2 = 1.0 * 10^10.) Tj
T*
(Fraction 2: N2 = 200, M2 = 20,000 => N2*M2 = 4,000,000; N2*M2^2 = 8.0 * 10^10.) Tj
T*
(Fraction 3: N3 = 100, M3 = 50,000 => N3*M3 = 5,000,000; N3*M3^2 = 25.0 * 10^10.) Tj
T*
(Sums: sum N_i = 400; sum \(N_i*M_i\) = 10,000,000; sum \(N_i*M_i^2\) = 34.0 * 10^10.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Number-Average Molecular Weight M_n:) Tj
T*
(M_n = sum \(N_i * M_i\) / sum N_i = 10,000,000 / 400 = 25,000 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Weight-Average Molecular Weight M_w:) Tj
T*
(M_w = sum \(N_i * M_i^2\) / sum \(N_i * M_i\) = 34.0 * 10^10 / 10,000,000 = 34,000 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Calculate Polydispersity Index \(PDI\):) Tj
T*
(PDI = M_w / M_n = 34,000 / 25,000 = 1.36.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Since PDI > 1.0, the polymer is polydisperse with moderate molecular weight) Tj
T*
(distribution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
