(Problem: A sample of Nylon-6,6 has a weight-average molecular weight of M_w = 45,200) Tj
T*
(g/mol. Calculate: \(1\) Molecular weight of the repeating structural unit, \(2\) Degree of) Tj
T*
(Polymerization \(DP\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Chemical Formula of Nylon-6,6 Repeating Unit:) Tj
T*
(Monomers: Adipic Acid \(HOOC-\(CH2\)4-COOH\) + Hexamethylenediamine \(H2N-\(CH2\)6-NH2\).) Tj
T*
(Condensation eliminates 2 H2O molecules per repeating unit:) Tj
T*
(Repeating Unit Formula: -[ NH-\(CH2\)6-NH-CO-\(CH2\)4-CO ]-.) Tj
T*
(Elemental Count: C12 H22 N2 O2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Molecular Weight of Repeating Unit M_0:) Tj
T*
(Carbon: 12 * 12.011 = 144.13 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Hydrogen: 22 * 1.008 = 22.18 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Nitrogen: 2 * 14.007 = 28.01 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Oxygen: 2 * 15.999 = 32.00 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(M_0 = 144.13 + 22.18 + 28.01 + 32.00 = 226.32 g/mol.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Degree of Polymerization \(DP\):) Tj
T*
(DP = M_w / M_0 = 45,200 / 226.32 = 199.7 ~ 200 repeating units.) Tj
