T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A spherical CdSe quantum dot of radius r = 2.0 nm has bulk band gap E_{g,bulk}) Tj
T*
(= 1.74 eV. Using the Brus quantum confinement equation:) Tj
T*
(E_g\(r\) = E_{g,bulk} + [ h^2 / \(8 * r^2\) ] * \(1/m_e* + 1/m_h*\) - [ 1.8 * e^2 /) Tj
T*
(\(4*pi*epsilon*r\) ].) Tj
T*
(Given effective mass factor \(1/m_e* + 1/m_h*\) = 8.5 * 10^30 kg^-1 and ignoring Coulomb) Tj
T*
(correction: Calculate: \(1\) Effective band gap E_g in eV, \(2\) Photoluminescence emission) Tj
T*
(wavelength lambda in nanometers.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Confinement Energy:) Tj
T*
(h = 6.626 * 10^-34 J*s; r = 2.0 * 10^-9 m.) Tj
T*
(Confinement = [ \(6.626 * 10^-34\)^2 / \(8 * \(2.0 * 10^-9\)^2\) ] * \(8.5 * 10^30\)) Tj
T*
(= [ 4.390 * 10^-67 / \(3.2 * 10^-17\) ] * \(8.5 * 10^30\) = \(1.372 * 10^-50\) * \(8.5 * 10^30\)) Tj
T*
(= 1.166 * 10^-19 Joules.) Tj
T*
(Convert to eV \(1 eV = 1.602 * 10^-19 J\): 1.166 * 10^-19 / 1.602 * 10^-19 = 0.728 eV.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Total Effective Band Gap:) Tj
T*
(E_g\(r\) = 1.74 eV + 0.728 eV = 2.468 eV.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Emission Wavelength lambda:) Tj
T*
(lambda = \(h * c\) / E_g = \(1240 eV*nm\) / 2.468 eV = 502.4 nm \(Green emission\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Decreasing quantum dot radius from bulk to 2 nm shifts emission into the) Tj
T*
(green visible spectrum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
