(fiber by volume \(V_f = 0.60, V_m = 0.40\). The elastic modulus of carbon fiber is E_f =) Tj
T*
(240 GPa; elastic modulus of epoxy matrix is E_m = 4.0 GPa. Calculate: \(1\) Longitudinal) Tj
T*
(modulus E_L \(isostrain\), \(2\) Transverse modulus E_T \(isostress\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Longitudinal Modulus E_L \(Rule of Mixtures\):) Tj
T*
(E_L = E_f * V_f + E_m * V_m = \(240 GPa * 0.60\) + \(4.0 GPa * 0.40\) = 144.0 + 1.6 = 145.6) Tj
T*
(GPa.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Transverse Modulus E_T \(Inverse Rule of Mixtures\):) Tj
T*
(1 / E_T = \(V_f / E_f\) + \(V_m / E_m\) = \(0.60 / 240\) + \(0.40 / 4.0\) = 0.0025 + 0.1000 =) Tj
T*
(0.1025 GPa^-1.) Tj
T*
(E_T = 1 / 0.1025 = 9.76 GPa.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: The composite exhibits dramatic mechanical anisotropy: E_L \(145.6 GPa\) is 15) Tj
T*
(times stronger than E_T \(9.76 GPa\).) Tj
