T*
(* Q1: Describe the synthesis, structure, and curing mechanism of Bakelite) Tj
T*
(\(Phenol-Formaldehyde resin\).) Tj
T*
(Answer: Synthesis proceeds in two stages: \(1\) Formation of prepolymers: Phenol and) Tj
T*
(Formaldehyde react in the presence of acid or alkali catalysts. Formaldehyde undergoes) Tj
T*
(electrophilic aromatic substitution on phenol at ortho and para positions, yielding) Tj
T*
(o-hydroxybenzyl alcohol and p-hydroxybenzyl alcohol. \(2\) Novolac vs. Resol: Acid) Tj
T*
(catalysis with excess phenol yields a linear, soluble, fusible thermoplastic polymer) Tj
T*
(called Novolac. Alkaline catalysis with excess formaldehyde yields branched Resols) Tj
T*
(containing reactive methylol \(-CH2OH\) groups. \(3\) Curing to Bakelite: When Novolac is) Tj
T*
(heated to 150-200 deg C with hexamethylenetetramine \(hexa\) and fillers, hexa decomposes) Tj
T*
(into formaldehyde and ammonia. The liberated formaldehyde forms rigid methylene \(-CH2-\)) Tj
T*
(bridges cross-linking Novolac chains into a hard, rigid, infusible, insoluble 3D) Tj
T*
(thermosetting polymer network.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the mechanism of electrical conduction in conducting polymers and) Tj
T*
(describe the role of p-doping and n-doping.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Pristine conjugated polymers like polyacetylene possess alternating single and) Tj
T*
(double carbon-carbon bonds with continuous overlap of pi-orbitals along the planar) Tj
T*
(backbone. However, Peierls instability opens a finite band gap \(~1.5 eV\), rendering them) Tj
T*
(semiconductors. Electrical conductivity is increased by orders of magnitude via chemical) Tj
T*
(or electrochemical doping. p-doping involves partial oxidation using electron acceptors) Tj
T*
(\(I2, AsF5, FeCl3\). An electron is removed from the pi-system, creating a localized) Tj
T*
(radical cation called a Polaron. Removal of a second electron yields a pair of like) Tj
T*
(charges called a Bipolaron. Under an applied electric field, these bipolarons delocalize) Tj
T*
(and migrate along the conjugated backbone via soliton/bipolaron hopping, achieving) Tj
T*
(metallic conductivities up to 10^5 S/cm. n-doping involves partial reduction using) Tj
T*
(alkali metals \(Na, K\), injecting electrons into the conduction band.) Tj
T*
